{{--
    Shared by both the "add rule" form and each existing rule's edit form
    below — included only while formula_type === 'custom_formula' is
    selected (the parent x-show wraps this), so it doesn't clutter the
    page for the other 4 built-in formula types that don't need it.

    Explains, in Vietnamese, exactly which product/context columns the
    "Công thức" expression may reference (with what each one actually
    means, not just its raw column name) versus the 2 columns that power
    the "Lấy phụ phí từ sản phẩm..." checkbox instead — an admin who
    doesn't recognise "base_price" or "length_cm" by name, or who might
    otherwise try typing "extra_fee" into the expression, gets the
    context to avoid both mistakes.
--}}
<div class="mt-3 rounded-md border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-3 text-xs text-amber-800">
    <p class="font-medium">Được dùng trong ô "Công thức" bên dưới (gõ đúng tên cột này):</p>
    <ul class="mt-1.5 list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        @foreach ($formulaVariableLabels as $variable => $label)
            <li><code class="rounded bg-white px-1 py-0.5">{{ $variable }}</code> — {{ $label }}</li>
        @endforeach
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-2">
        Ví dụ: <code class="rounded bg-white px-1 py-0.5">base_price + length_cm * 5000</code>.
        Gõ tên cột khác ngoài danh sách trên sẽ bị báo lỗi khi lưu.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-3 font-medium">Không gõ vào ô "Công thức" — 2 cột này chỉ dùng qua checkbox "Lấy phụ phí từ sản phẩm..." bên dưới:</p>
    <ul class="mt-1.5 list-disc space-y-1 pl-4">
        @foreach ($extraFeeVariableLabels as $variable => $label)
            <li><code class="rounded bg-white px-1 py-0.5">{{ $variable }}</code> — {{ $label }}</li>
        @endforeach
    </ul>
</div>
